    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d509">

                <pb facs="0627" n="547" sameAs="frus:frus1901/pg547"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Russell to Mr. Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Caracas</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1901-06-15"><hi rendition="#italic">June 15,
                        1901.</hi></date></dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 629.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inform you that on the
                    9th instant a cable was received by the President of Venezuela from the governor
                    of the island of Margarita, notifying him that an American man-of-war
                    (presumably the <hi rendition="#italic">Mayflower</hi>) was anchored off the
                    port of Juan Griego, but had not entered.</p>
                <p>The President has cabled for details regarding the arrival and anchorage of the
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Mayflower.</hi></p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">William W.
                    Russell.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
